        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: avaliar",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "avaliar — \"to evaluate, to assess\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "O professor avalia os alunos todas as semanas. The teacher assesses the pupils every week."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also to value: avaliar uma casa — to value a house."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "avaliar is built on valia \"value, worth\", from the verb valer, which is inherited from Latin valēre \"to be strong, to be worth\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
